+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

This port follows the pinned prerelease source and has no pledge or unveil
policy. Run it with the permissions and destination directory appropriate
for the archive being processed; there is no process sandbox.

The tar library skips entries containing parent-directory components.
The port reports those skipped unsafe paths as extraction errors rather
than returning success for an incomplete extraction. This does not make
extraction transactional: earlier entries may already have been written.

Archive paths, links, file permissions and extraction into directories
writable by other users still require native regression validation.
